  "notes": [
    "The C++ unit test strict-parses this manifest and binds its identity, version, exact case order, expected error codes and branch-sensitive detail markers before executing every documented case.",
    "Fixtures are generated at test runtime and contain no real loci, read names or production payload.",
    "The positive case intentionally contains old/new stable transitions; historical stable churn is reported as COMPARABLE_DIFFERENT and is not confused with the required w24/w40 semantic determinism.",
    "Native TSV negatives cover missing, wrong and out-of-order metadata plus duplicate headers before any scientific counter can be trusted.",
    "Co-occurrence negatives cover worker-count replay parity, duplicate/out-of-order primary keys, checked aggregate overflow, the frozen endpoint-A, family and joint-signature vocabularies, family/exact-status compatibility, BY/BH/formal subset hierarchy, FDR family-size binding, pair/site aggregate conservation and joint/topology-unit conservation.",
    "A focused positive fixture proves that an empty exact FDR family is legal: fdr_family_size, BH, BY, formal, joint PASS and topology units are all zero and w24 equals w40.",
    "The positive fixture deliberately has one topology unit and two topology regions; units and regions are different grains, while complete plus incomplete regions still conserves topology_regions.",
    "Every negative fixture rebuilds its own hashes and receipt chain and asserts its expected_error_code; branch-sensitive cases also assert expected_detail_contains so an earlier generic failure cannot satisfy the oracle."
